static const struct {const char *title,*hint,*answer;} guideTips[] = {{"Why did the POK\u00e9MON on this route change?","Look at the clock.","The game has four times of day on its clock: morning from 5 AM, day from 9 AM, evening from 5 PM and night from 9 PM. Grass and caves have a list for the morning, the day and the night, and the evening uses the night's. HERE shows the list for the time your game's clock says."},{"Why are the wild POK\u00e9MON here close to my level?","It depends on your badges.","Some side areas set their wild POK\u00e9MON's levels by how many badges you have, among them the coasts off ROUTE 32 to 35, QUIET CAVE, YELLOW FOREST and the ORANGE ISLANDS. HERE already shows the levels for the badges you hold."},{"Why does surfing find higher levels than HERE's slot says?","","While surfing, a wild POK\u00e9MON is often one to four levels over its slot's level. HERE's levels for SURFING include that."},{"Why do some trees never have the rare POK\u00e9MON?","It has to do with your trainer ID.","Each tree you HEADBUTT is common, rare or almost empty, picked from where the tree stands and your trainer ID. HERE lists both tables; try every tree on a route to find the rare ones."},{"Which rod catches what at the shore?","","On the shore's GOOD ROD and SUPER ROD lists one slot changes with the clock: CORSOLA in the morning and day, STARYU in the evening and at night. HERE shows the one for now."},{"Is the POK\u00e9MON LEAGUE harder the second time?","Come back with every badge.","With all 16 badges, the ELITE FOUR and LANCE use much stronger teams. NEXT BOSS lists them after the Kanto gyms."},{"What does RED give me?","A key item.","After the battle in SILVER CAVE, RED hands you the MYSTICTICKET. Show it at the ferry gate in VERMILION CITY for a trip to an island with one more trainer waiting at its top."}};
